[{:seon.task/name "ns-keeps-its-metadata"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by session AGENTS working as a Seon agent (2026-10-21), and earlier by N1: Jolt's (ns ^:scratch foo) does not attach :scratch (or any metadata) to the namespace, so the \"declared ^:scratch\" namespace seon.program describes cannot be declared from the REPL; only seon.agent/make-ns! sets it, through alter-meta! (agent.clj:350), and seon.program/recording reapplies ns metadata as a stopgap (program.clj:125). On the JVM, (meta (find-ns 'foo)) holds the ns form's metadata. Fix in our Jolt fork's ns macro / host/chez/ns.ss (a jolt/<topic> branch): the ns form's metadata (and docstring, attr-map) merges on the namespace; then the stopgap and make-ns!'s alter-meta! go (every definition happens once)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.program-test/a-scratch-ns-declared-at-the-repl-stays-scratch}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-built-binary-requires-a-stdlib-namespace-it-did-not-compile"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by session TESTS (2026-10-21) importing test/ into a root: in a root booted from target/seon (cd target, ./seon root), `(require 'fipp.engine)` answers `Could not locate clojure/core/rrb_vector.jolt (or .clj/.cljc) on the source roots`, and `(vec (jolt.host/source-roots))` is [\"./src\" \"./resources\" \"./reference-code/persistent-sorted-set/src\" \"jolt-core\" \"stdlib\" \"vendor/fs/src\" ...]: relative paths, resolved against the process's cwd (target/), where none exists. clojure.core.rrb-vector is Jolt's own stdlib (reference-code/jolt/stdlib/clojure/core/rrb_vector.clj), so a binary can require only what it compiled in, while bin/test (the runtime with deps resolved) loads it. It blocks `seon.source/the-tests-are-part-of-the-program`: `seon.print-test` requires `fipp.engine` (the layout's test oracle), so a root with `:seon.config.source/dirs [\"src\" \"test\"]` fails at boot, and an agent's fork could not run that test either. Correct: a built binary resolves a library it did not compile the way the runtime does (its stdlib embedded or found by absolute path, its deps' roots recorded at build), or the binary's build compiles what test/ requires; which one is a Jolt build decision for root (a dependency change waits for root's go). Then rerun the boot with run1.edn's dirs. Done by session J1 (2026-10-21) the way Jolt's design already assumed (docs/forks.md, jolt section, `jolt/embed-stdlib`): `jolt build` gives an app that keeps the compiler jolt's install sources as one blob constant in its runtime unit (build.ss `bld-emit-install-sources`, io.ss `jolt-source-blob-attach-bytes!`); absolute roots were not taken, because Jolt's loader probes embedded keys first and #1232 made a binary independent of the build machine's paths. Measured on target/seon: binary 205.61 -> 206.51 MB, `seon ports` 0.63 -> 0.61 s, max RSS +1.9 MB, a root's boot with src 2.86 -> 2.78 s and with src and test 3.7 s (before: refused), `(require 'clojure.core.rrb-vector)` 6 ms and `fipp.engine` 30 ms from any cwd. Open: such a namespace compiles from source in every process (install-owned and embedded files are not AOT-cached); a cost only if a large one is reached."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.root-test/a-root-binary-requires-a-library-it-did-not-compile}}
 {:seon.task/name "whole-program-inference-keeps-nil-checks"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by root 2026-10-21: in the built binary (whole-program inference on), `seon.ref/line-citation` throws `parse-long requires a string: ` for `src/a.clj:50`, while `src/a.clj:5-9` works and `bin/test` (uncompiled) passes `seon.ref-test/a-line-citation-is-its-file-marked-line-reference`. The function destructures `[from to]` from `(if dash [a b] [suffix])` and tests `(or (nil? to) (parse-long to))`: the compiled code calls `parse-long` with `to` nil, as if `(nil? to)` were folded to false because `to` is inferred a string from the first branch only. Effect: `my.root/load-tasks!` fails on any task file whose text cites `path:N` (four shipped entries do), so a built root cannot load task files. Correct: Jolt's inference types a destructured binding from every branch (here string-or-nil) and never folds a `nil?` test it cannot prove; fixed in Jolt on a `jolt/<topic>` branch with a Jolt-level reproduction, or whole-program inference left off for the open-world root (BUILD plan P3 decides by measurement). Proof: a root binary resolves `seon.ref/line-citation` for `path:50`. Cause (session WPI, 2026-10-21): not the whole-program pass; `JOLT_NO_WP_INFER=1` builds fold it too. Jolt's intra-procedural inference (`jolt.passes.types/infer-call`) typed every element read (`nth`, `first`, `second`, `peek`, `last`, `fnext`) off a typed vector as the element, and `jolt.passes.types/pred-on` folds `nil?` false on any concrete scalar. Destructuring `[from to]` reads `(nth v 1 nil)`, so `to` was `:str` and `(nil? to)` became false. Fixed in Jolt `jolt/infer-nil-union`: the read joins the element with the default (`nth`'s 3-arity) or `:nil` (the others); proof build-smoke's elem-nil case."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.root-test/a-built-root-reads-a-line-citation}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-build-without-whole-program-inference-compiles-tools-reader"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by session INPLACE, reproduced by session WPI (2026-10-21, Jolt `be2495af`): `JOLT_NO_WP_INFER=1 bin/build seon` fails in 11 s with `error[analyze/internal-failure]: variable jv$clojure.tools.reader.impl.utils/<=clojure-1-7-alpha5 is not bound` (tools.reader 1.5.2 `clojure.tools.reader.impl.utils`, its `compile-when` over `<=clojure-1-7-alpha5`). The smallest case is `test/build/build/reader.clj` (requires `clojure.tools.reader`): built with `-A:hello` it builds and prints `[1 2]` with whole-program inference on, and fails as above with it off; `build.hello` (Datahike, no tools.reader require) builds either way. Cause (session REDS, 2026-10-22): the build publishes a fresh compilation unit with direct-linking on (host/chez/build.ss ~2481-2492) and the emit walk registers each emitted def in it (jolt-core/jolt/backend_scheme.clj:4370); `direct-linkable?` (backend_scheme.clj:485) then links a reference to that def's jv$ variable, which exists only in the emitted text. `compile-when` evals its condition at expansion through `jolt-analyze-emit-form` (host/chez/compile-eval.ss:521), against the build's unit, so once the def was emitted the eval references an unbound jv$. Whole-program inference (`bld-wp-infer!`) expands every macro before any def is emitted, which hid it; the emit walk without it analyzes each form after the earlier defs were emitted. Fix on Jolt branch `jolt/eval-outside-build` (d7ec259b): the build records the process's unit before it (`ce-build-unit-enter!`) and the process's own analyze-and-eval compiles against that unit with the build's optimize and direct-link flags off (`ce-outside-build`); build-smoke case eval-at-expansion builds and runs with inference on and off. Root bumps the pin at merge. Note: Jolt reads the switch with `getenv`, so an empty `JOLT_NO_WP_INFER=` also turns inference off. Correct: the build without whole-program inference compiles every namespace the inference build compiles (BUILD plan P3 needs it to measure an open-world root). Fixed in Jolt on a `jolt/<topic>` branch with a build-smoke case."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.root-test/a-build-without-whole-program-inference-reads-with-tools-reader}}]
